--- clean-app/CHANGELOG.md	2026-11-26 10:01:16.135190632 +0000
+++ week6/app/CHANGELOG.md	2026-11-26 15:50:34.782129072 +0000
@@ -2,6 +2,12 @@
 
 Dates are the day a release finished rolling out to production.
 
+## Unreleased (INC-2231)
+
+- router: an endpoint's version is compared only with versions the api assigned (version 3 messages). A version 2 `endpoint` message carries a sequence number, not an api version; it orders only against other version 2 messages, only for endpoints the api has not spoken for, and never overrides the api. Previously such a message raised the stored version (to its `seq`), so every later change from the api was dropped as stale, and a late one could undo a change the api had accepted.
+- router: the `endpoints` table gains `api_version`. Existing rows get 0, so the next version 3 message for an endpoint always applies.
+- api: on its first start after this release the api publishes every endpoint's current configuration once (`meta` key `resync:INC-2231`), so changes the router dropped take effect without merchants repeating them. Touches api and router, hence this note.
+
 ## 2.3.1 (2026-08-14)
 
 - router: workaround for INC-2188 behind a flag, `SWITCHYARD_INC2188_WORKAROUND`, on unless set to `off`.
